VALUES ('RTX', 'published', '{"ticker":"RTX","reviewed":"August 2, 2026","completeness":100,"newsroomUrl":"https://www.rtx.com/news","description":"Aerospace and defense company spanning aircraft engines, avionics, missiles, sensors, space, cyber, and aftermarket services.","lede":"RTX Corp. earns owner value through long-cycle government and commercial contracts, original-equipment sales, cost-plus and fixed-price programs, and aftermarket services. The three questions that matter most are flight hours, shop visits, parts pricing, installed base, and spare engines, awards, funded backlog, mix, deliveries, and program margin, engine inspections, removals, compensation, supplier recovery, and cash cost.","sells":"Commercial and military engines, avionics, mission systems, missiles, radars, sensors, space systems, and maintenance.","revenueModel":"Long-cycle government and commercial contracts, original-equipment sales, cost-plus and fixed-price programs, and aftermarket services.","opportunity":"Commercial flight hours, defense replenishment, modernization, and backlog conversion can drive revenue and cash flow.","mustGoRight":"Powder-metal remediation must remain bounded, suppliers must support output, fixed-price programs must execute, and cash must convert.","editorNote":"Treat the claimed advantage—large installed bases, certified platforms, engineering depth, and classified capabilities can support durable aftermarket and program revenue.—as a thesis to verify against filings, cash conversion, customer behavior, and competitor evidence rather than as an established fact.","bullTitle":"What can compound owner value","bull":["Large installed bases, certified platforms, engineering depth, and classified capabilities can support durable aftermarket and program revenue.","Commercial flight hours, defense replenishment, modernization, and backlog conversion can drive revenue and cash flow.","Visible progress in commercial aftermarket and defense backlog can improve the durability and quality of earnings.","Disciplined reinvestment and capital allocation can convert operating progress into per-share value."],"bearTitle":"What can impair the thesis","bear":["Engine quality and safety can weaken the owner outcome; monitor inspection findings, removals, compensation, regulatory action, and cash charges.","Fixed-price programs can weaken the owner outcome; monitor estimate-at-completion changes, milestones, schedule, and loss provisions.","Supply-chain constraints can weaken the owner outcome; monitor castings, electronics, labor, inventory, and supplier health.","A valuation that assumes flawless execution can fall even when the underlying business remains viable."],"thesisBreaker":"The thesis breaks if quality remediation and program charges repeatedly consume the cash expected from commercial aerospace recovery and defense backlog.","financialDrivers":[{"label":"COMMERCIAL AFTERMARKET","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"flight hours, shop visits, parts pricing, installed base, and spare engines"},{"label":"DEFENSE BACKLOG","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"awards, funded backlog, mix, deliveries, and program margin"},{"label":"QUALITY REMEDIATION","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"engine inspections, removals, compensation, supplier recovery, and cash cost"},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Capacity and resilience","detail":"Liquidity, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, interest cost, and refinancing exposure."},{"label":"CASH CONVERSION","value":"Earnings quality","detail":"Operating cash flow, working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, restructuring, and normalized free cash flow."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner conversion","detail":"Diluted shares, stock compensation, repurchases, dividends, retained earnings, and return on invested capital."}],"risks":[{"title":"Engine quality and safety","level":"High","text":"Engine quality and safety can materially reduce revenue durability, margins, cash con