VALUES ('GEV', 'published', '{"ticker":"GEV","reviewed":"August 2, 2026","completeness":100,"newsroomUrl":"https://www.gevernova.com/news","description":"Energy-equipment and services company spanning power generation, wind, and grid technologies.","lede":"GE VERNOVA Inc. earns owner value through equipment and project sales, long-term service agreements, parts, upgrades, software, and grid-system contracts. The three questions that matter most are gas orders, service agreements, upgrades, delivery, and margin, grid orders, backlog, capacity, project execution, and working capital, onshore pricing, offshore losses, warranty, blade quality, and cash burn.","sells":"Gas turbines, steam and nuclear equipment, wind turbines, grid hardware and software, services, and upgrades.","revenueModel":"Equipment and project sales, long-term service agreements, parts, upgrades, software, and grid-system contracts.","opportunity":"Electricity demand, grid modernization, gas generation, nuclear service, and wind restructuring can expand profitable backlog.","mustGoRight":"Backlog must convert without cost overruns, wind losses must decline, and capacity investment must earn attractive returns.","editorNote":"Treat the claimed advantage—a large installed base, service capability, and scarce grid and generation engineering can benefit from rising power investment.—as a thesis to verify against filings, cash conversion, customer behavior, and competitor evidence rather than as an established fact.","bullTitle":"What can compound owner value","bull":["A large installed base, service capability, and scarce grid and generation engineering can benefit from rising power investment.","Electricity demand, grid modernization, gas generation, nuclear service, and wind restructuring can expand profitable backlog.","Visible progress in power backlog and electrification can improve the durability and quality of earnings.","Disciplined reinvestment and capital allocation can convert operating progress into per-share value."],"bearTitle":"What can impair the thesis","bear":["Long-cycle project execution can weaken the owner outcome; monitor cost estimates, milestones, liquidated damages, and working capital.","Wind warranty and offshore exposure can weaken the owner outcome; monitor provisions, claims, cancellations, and cash payments.","Supply and capacity can weaken the owner outcome; monitor lead times, factory investment, suppliers, labor, and customer deposits.","A valuation that assumes flawless execution can fall even when the underlying business remains viable."],"thesisBreaker":"The thesis breaks if project execution and wind liabilities consume the cash generated by power and electrification franchises.","financialDrivers":[{"label":"POWER BACKLOG","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"gas orders, service agreements, upgrades, delivery, and margin"},{"label":"ELECTRIFICATION","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"grid orders, backlog, capacity, project execution, and working capital"},{"label":"WIND RECOVERY","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"onshore pricing, offshore losses, warranty, blade quality, and cash burn"},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Capacity and resilience","detail":"Liquidity, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, interest cost, and refinancing exposure."},{"label":"CASH CONVERSION","value":"Earnings quality","detail":"Operating cash flow, working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, restructuring, and normalized free cash flow."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner conversion","detail":"Diluted shares, stock compensation, repurchases, dividends, retained earnings, and return on invested capital."}],"risks":[{"title":"Long-cycle project execution","level":"High","text":"Long-cycle project execution can materially reduce revenue durability, margins, cash conversion, or the value of invested capital.","signal":"cost estimates, milestones, liquidated damages, and working capital"},{"title":"Wind warranty and offshore expos