iably verifies analog demand?","What would cause 300mm capacity to structurally improve or deteriorate?","How should owners separate cyclical movement from durable change in free cash flow?","Where does TEXAS INSTRUMENT Inc. have the greatest unpriced customer, supplier, or regulatory dependency?","Which management commitment is most important to verify in the next two reporting periods?","What measurable development would invalidate the owner thesis rather than merely create short-term volatility?"],"competitors":"ANALOG DEVICES INC, NXP Semiconductors N.V., MICROCHIP TECHNOLOGY INC, ON SEMICONDUCTOR CORP, STM, MONOLITHIC POWER SYSTEMS INC","comparables":[{"name":"ANALOG DEVICES INC","ticker":"ADI","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Operating and valuation reference for TXN","valuation":"Use current enterprise value, earnings, cash flow, and sector-appropriate multiples; normalize accounting, leverage, and capital intensity.","financialStatus":"Compare growth, margins, balance-sheet capacity, cash conversion, and competitive position with TXN.","sourceUrl":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0000006281&owner=exclude"},{"name":"NXP Semiconductors N.V.","ticker":"NXPI","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Operating and valuation reference for TXN","valuation":"Use current enterprise value, earnings, cash flow, and sector-appropriate multiples; normalize accounting, leverage, and capital intensity.","financialStatus":"Compare growth, margins, balance-sheet capacity, cash conversion, and competitive position with TXN.","sourceUrl":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001413447&owner=exclude"},{"name":"MICROCHIP TECHNOLOGY INC","ticker":"MCHP","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Operating and valuation reference for TXN","valuation":"Use current enterprise value, earnings, cash flow, and sector-appropriate multiples; normalize accounting, leverage, and capital intensity.","financialStatus":"Compare growth, margins, balance-sheet capacity, cash conversion, and c