ting progress into per-share value."],"bearTitle":"What can impair the thesis","bear":["Project and customer exposure can weaken the owner outcome; monitor cost, schedule, take-or-pay terms, counterparty credit, and utilization.","Energy and currency can weaken the owner outcome; monitor pass-through, power and feedstock cost, hedging, and translation.","Industrial cycle can weaken the owner outcome; monitor volumes, plant utilization, customer shutdowns, and merchant pricing.","A valuation that assumes flawless execution can fall even when the underlying business remains viable."],"thesisBreaker":"The thesis breaks if capital-heavy projects repeatedly earn inadequate returns or contract protections fail during customer distress and energy volatility.","financialDrivers":[{"label":"ON-SITE PROJECTS","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"backlog, startup, contract terms, volumes, customer credit, and returns"},{"label":"PRICE & PRODUCTIVITY","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"pricing, energy pass-through, density, plant utilization, and cost savings"},{"label":"ELECTRONICS & CLEAN ENERGY","value":"Primary owner KPI","detail":"project sanctions, customer ramps, subsidies, hydrogen, and specialty-gas demand"},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Capacity and resilience","detail":"Liquidity, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, interest cost, and refinancing exposure."},{"label":"CASH CONVERSION","value":"Earnings quality","detail":"Operating cash flow, working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, restructuring, and normalized free cash flow."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner conversion","detail":"Diluted shares, stock compensation, repurchases, dividends, retained earnings, and return on invested capital."}],"risks":[{"title":"Project and customer exposure","level":"High","text":"Project and customer exposure can materially reduce revenue durability, margins, cash conversion, or the value of invested capital.","signal":"cost, schedule, take-or-pay terms, 